/target
/.qlever-venv
/bench/native-qlever/
# Competitor gather output (scripts/gather-competitors.sh) — regenerable, never committed.
/bench/competitor-results/
# MPC heavy/ceiling matrix output (scripts/mpc-ec2-ceiling.sh, sq-hoaj) — measured
# Tier-3 wall-clock envelopes; regenerable, never committed (no-hard-coded-perf rule).
/bench/mpc-ceiling-results/
# RIF full-suite pass-rate output (bench/rif/run.sh over the fetched W3C archive) —
# regenerable, never committed (pass/fail counts belong in run output, not markdown).
/bench/rif/results.tsv
# SCALED matched-workload RSP replay (sq-3f5ay) — ~10^5 lines, deterministically
# regenerated by `bench/rsp/rsp4j_compare.py gen-replay`. The PIN is the generator plus
# bench/rsp/replay/scaled.manifest.json (params + sha256), which IS committed; the
# payload never is. The small oracle replays (replay/*.ts.tsv) stay committed.
/bench/rsp/replay/scaled_srbench.ts.tsv
# K4 compose A/B regenerable scratch (per-prompt + per-judge .txt, batch splits, logs) —
# regenerated by compose_k4 + assemble.py; the answers_*/scores_*/k4_result.json ARE committed.
/bench/compose/k4/prompts/
/bench/compose/k4/judge/
/bench/compose/k4/batch_*
/bench/compose/k4/jbatch_*
/bench/compose/k4/all_*.txt
/bench/compose/k4/gen.log
/dist
# Local AWS hwbench scratch (keys/results) — never committed.
/.sparq-hwbench/
# W3C conformance test data (fetched by scripts/fetch-conformance.sh) — never committed.
/tests/w3c/
# SolidLab ODRL Test Suite data (fetched by scripts/fetch-odrl-suite.sh) — never committed.
/tests/odrl-test-suite/
# Conformance scoreboard (regenerated locally by `cargo run -p sparq-conformance`).
/conformance-report.md
# NOTE [OPUS-4.8] sq-l8imt: inference-conformance-report.md is INTENTIONALLY tracked —
# AGENTS.md §Conformance states "the inference report is committed at
# inference-conformance-report.md". The earlier `/inference-conformance-report.md` ignore
# rule here was a bug: it made the committed file tracked-AND-ignored, which release-plz's
# (cargo) VCS dirty-check treated as an uncommitted change and aborted Release-PR (sq-owci).
# Do NOT re-add an ignore rule for this path.
# Consolidated cross-crate scoreboard (regenerated by `cargo run -p sparq-conformance --bin sparq-conformance-scoreboard`).
/conformance-scoreboard.md
# Local venv for the Python bindings (crates/sparq-py: maturin develop + pytest).
/.venv-py/
__pycache__/
# roborev snapshots
/.roborev/
STATUS.md

# [OPUS-4.8] sq-jpki.1 — repo-root npm workspaces: the SINGLE source of truth is the
# repo-root /package-lock.json (tracked). Per-workspace-member lockfiles are redundant and
# must never be committed — they would drift from the root lock. scripts/gen-js-sbom.sh
# transiently DERIVES js/package-lock.json from the root lock (and removes it on exit); pin
# these paths ignored so a stray member lock can never re-enter the tree.
/js/package-lock.json
/site/package-lock.json
/gui/e2e/package-lock.json
/packages/*/package-lock.json

# [OPUS-4.8] sq-1bc9 — repo-root npm-workspaces installs hoist deps into the ROOT
# node_modules/ (and members keep their own). Only some members ship a node_modules
# .gitignore line (js/site/gui-e2e do; packages/sparq-client does NOT), and the repo
# root had none — so a root `npm ci` left node_modules/ untracked and stageable.
# Ignore node_modules everywhere (unanchored — covers the root + every nested member) plus
# an explicit packages/*/node_modules/ so an installed dep can never be accidentally staged.
node_modules/
/packages/*/node_modules/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (transient scratch; the tracked skills under .claude/skills/ stay)
/.claude/worktrees/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
# [OPUS-4.8] Scope the Dolt/SQLite ignore to .beads/ so legitimate *.db
# fixtures elsewhere in the tree are NOT silently hidden from `git add`.
# (The generated DBs live under .beads/, which also ships its own .gitignore.)
.dolt/
.beads/*.db
.beads/*.db-journal
.beads/*.db-wal
.beads/*.db-shm
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# [OPUS-4.8] Agent-metrics RUNTIME rows (bead sq-lhwo.1): per-PR/per-task metrics
# rows carry NON-CANONICAL session-local numbers (and may reference session
# transcripts), so the live append-only log is git-ignored. The COMMITTED data is the
# reproducible cross-PR baseline at metrics/baseline.jsonl (GitHub/git/roborev-derived
# columns only — no session tokens), which is regenerable via capture_baseline.py.
metrics/runtime/

# KB dump output (scripts/export-kb-dump.py, sq-tzars.8) — assembled locally then pushed
# to sparq-org/research-kb; never committed to this repo.  A leak-abort leaves partial
# content in this directory, so git-ignoring it prevents accidental staging.
/dumps/

# Local tool binaries (e.g. a session-installed cargo-nextest) — opaque executables are
# unreviewable and a supply-chain risk; install tools via the pinned CI/dev bootstrap
# instead. Ignored so one can never be accidentally committed (PR #3453 review).
/.local-bin/
